  "source": "data/v1 Opp Decks/Challenge 1 Opponent Decks v1.xlsx — Trevor's workbook, the fifth hand-built roster and the first that is not a set. Sheets 'Grass' through 'Colorless', one per Energy type.",
  "retrieved": "2026-09-01, Job 15a, read through tools/lib/xlsx.js.",
  "scope": "The Challenge 1 bracket: seven mono-type decks drawn from Base Set, Jungle and Fossil plus the promos those brackets open. NOT a set — see CHALLENGES.md on why a Challenge bracket belongs to none.",
  "status": "All seven validate clean against Engine.prototype.validateDeck: 60 cards, no errors, no warnings, 4-copy limit respected, every card implemented. ONE id correction was needed — see `corrections` below, and note that no validator could have caught it: a deck of the wrong Energy is a perfectly legal 60-card deck.",
  "tier": "ALL SEVEN ARE TIER 4 and that is deliberate rather than a shortcut. Trevor, 1 Sep 2026: a Challenge is a boss round end to end, so there is no intro/body/gate shape here and no T1 faucet rung. See OPPONENTS.md.",
  "weights": "featureWeight is Trevor's own scoring, totalled. Comparable WITHIN this workbook only — the seven run 16.5 to 21, and Colorless at 21 is why Wigglytuff leads. Do not compare against Fossil's 11.5/16/19. See ROSTERS.md.",
  "pressure": "Derived from this workbook's Index tab by copy count, first code where a card lists several. Reported, not enforced — OPPONENTS.md's no-repeat rule is still unbuilt.",
  "coverCard": "The sheet's own Cover Card field. Grass's cell is blank in the workbook; Trevor named Vileplume on 1 Sep 2026.",
  "promos": "Four of the seven name promo cards. That is legal for an AUTHORED opponent deck and illegal for a GENERATED one — see opponentDeckFor() in ui.js.",
  "corrections": "ONE ID CORRECTION, and it is the first in five workbooks — 1 Sep 2026, found by Trevor PLAYING the deck. The Fire sheet's Energy row reads \"F Energy\" against id base1-97, which is FIGHTING Energy; Fire is base1-98. Trevor's own diagnosis: \"I wrote F energy instead of R energy in the deck list.\" In this era's shorthand F is Fighting and R is Fire, and the label and the id agreed with each other while both disagreed with the deck. Corrected to base1-98 HERE rather than in the workbook, which is Trevor's file — tell him so the source can be fixed too. THE EFFECT WAS TOTAL: 12 of the deck's 21 Pokemon could not pay for a single one of their attacks, and c1_fire measured 20.2% in decksim, the weakest deck ever recorded in ROSTERS.md. See the stranded-card guard in tools/progresstest.js, which exists because of this."
 }
